# Who may put what in MAIL FROM, for [% domain %].
#
# smtpd_sender_login_maps, enforced by reject_authenticated_sender_login_mismatch
# in smtpd_sender_restrictions.  An authenticated client whose MAIL FROM address
# is not owned by its SASL login name is rejected -- and an address missing from
# here has no owner at all, so it is rejected too.  That is why this is built
# from the accounts and the aliases together rather than by hand.
#
# The login name is the full address: that is what the dovecot passwd file this
# pairs with is keyed on.
#
# Unauthenticated senders are not checked against this.  They come in on port 25
# claiming to be anybody, and deciding what to do about that is DMARC's job, not
# a table's.
[% FOR login IN sender_logins %]
[% login.address %] [% login.owner %]
[%- END %]
